# Atlassian authoring (Confluence & Jira)

When creating or updating content via Atlassian MCP (Confluence pages, Jira issues, comments, transitions), **always prefix human-visible attribution text with `[Anna]`**.

## Apply to

| Action | Field / place | Example |
|--------|----------------|---------|
| Confluence page update | `versionMessage` | `[Anna] add confirmed routes from live exploration` |
| Jira issue comment | comment body (first line or summary) | `[Anna] Verified on staging; still reproduces.` |
| Jira issue create/edit | description lead-in when adding agent-authored summary | `[Anna] …` then details |
| New Confluence page | optional first paragraph or version message | `[Anna] Initial draft from live exploration` |

## Format

- Use the literal prefix **`[Anna]`** (square brackets, capital A).
- Follow with a space, then a short verb phrase in sentence case.
- Do **not** use alternate forms (`Anna:`, `P7:`, bare name) for version messages or comments unless the user explicitly asks for a different format in that turn.

## Scope

- Required for **writes** (create/update/comment/transition with comment).
- Not required for read-only lookups (`getJiraIssue`, `getConfluenceContent`, search).
